{%- comment -%}
  Brand-level rating badge for the product page.

  This replaces the Judge.me per-product preview badge, which showed whatever that one
  product had collected - "2 reviews" at three stars on Pistachio Truffles, five stars on
  Peanut Butter. A near-empty rating in the most prominent position on the page is a
  weaker signal than no rating at all.

  IMPORTANT - the number here must be the real store-wide average, and the label has to
  say so. A figure that reads as *this product's* rating when it is actually the store
  average is a misleading review claim under UAE consumer protection rules and the
  equivalent EU/UK ones. Hence:

    - the value comes from shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating, which Judge.me
      maintains, not from a number typed into a theme setting;
    - the copy says "across all Plaay products", not "this product";
    - if the metafield is missing, nothing renders. There is no hardcoded fallback,
      deliberately.

  If the badge is not appearing, the store-wide metafields are not published. In the
  Judge.me admin, install the "All Reviews" widget / page - that is what creates
  shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating and all_reviews_count.

  The badge links to #plaay-reviews, which is the pdp-social-proof section. That section
  currently holds hand-written testimonials; the honest destination is the Judge.me
  "Reviews" app block. Drop it into the product template at that anchor in the theme
  editor and the link points at real reviews.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Judge.me's store-wide metafields first. They are the live figure and cannot go stale.
    If they are not published, fall back to the two theme settings under Reviews - a
    stand-in the merchant keeps in step with the Judge.me dashboard. Both blank means no
    badge; there is no number baked into this file.
  endcomment
  assign rating = shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating
  assign rating_count = shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_count

  if rating == blank or rating_count == blank
    assign rating = settings.store_rating_value
    assign rating_count = settings.store_rating_count
  endif
-%}

{%- assign rating_value = rating | times: 1.0 -%}
{%- assign count_value = rating_count | times: 1 -%}

{%- if rating_value > 0 and count_value > 0 -%}
  {%- assign rating_rounded = rating_value | round: 1 -%}
  {%- assign full_stars = rating_value | floor -%}

  <a
    href="#plaay-reviews"
    class="plaay-rating-badge"
    data-plaay-scroll-to="#plaay-reviews"
    aria-label="{{ rating_rounded }} out of 5 from {{ rating_count }} reviews across all Plaay products. Jump to reviews.">
    <span class="plaay-rating-badge__stars" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
        <span class="plaay-rating-badge__star{% if forloop.index <= full_stars %} is-on{% endif %}">
          {%- render 'icon-star' -%}
        </span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </span>
    <span class="plaay-rating-badge__value font-walsheim-black">{{ rating_rounded }}</span>
    <span class="plaay-rating-badge__meta">
      {{ rating_count }} reviews across all Plaay products
    </span>
  </a>
{%- endif -%}
